  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PERFORMANCE-BASED PARTNERSHIP SCHEME FOCUSING ON QUALITY PROGRAMMING, UNDERSTANDING CHANGE AND RESULTS FOR POOR HOUSEHOLDS AND COMMUNITIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Women&#x2019;s Rights Programme in Ethiopia, implemented by ActionAid and local partners aims to contribute to the reduction of GBV by increasing feelings of safety among marginalised women and greater access to services. The main objective is for marginalised women to to access quality services that are accessible, appropriate and responsive to their needs and wishes.  Objective: Women can access quality services that are accessible, appropriate and survivor-centred. Outcome: Marginalised women and girls are feeling safer, able to access services and are claiming their rights to protection and participation</narrative>
  </description>
